From 70f4eadfbee51263820e9f22a93b6cfce3f388da Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kob <kob@invalid>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 23:49:21 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 05/13] Hard stream-first bound: playback lane, bounded
 background work while playback is active

Playback requests without a lane of their own share Lane::STREAM, so they never
pipeline behind another lane's unfinished reply. While a playback request is in
Pool::fetch, and for STREAM_LINGER (2 s) after the last one, background work
(Queue, Health, Warm):
- leaves min(max(4, playback requests), limit / 4) connections to playback,
  letting connections drain when it holds more;
- pipelines at most 2 deep, never onto a playback connection;
- takes no connection while a playback request holds a slot and waits for one.
Without playback, scheduling is unchanged.

Loopback (8 connections, depth 4, 100 ms reply delay, 8 MB/s per connection,
700 KB articles, saturating Queue load), 40 playback reads in 4-read seeks:
before p50 867 / p95 870 / p99 870 ms, after 286 / 480 / 480 ms; Queue
25.1 MB/s alone, 22.3 MB/s while seeking.
